# Cubic — Environment Variables

## Local development

### server/.env

```
PORT=5000
NODE_ENV=development
CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173

# MongoDB Atlas
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<db_username>:<db_password>@cluster.mongodb.net/cubic?appName=Cubic

# JWT (use long random strings in production)
JWT_ACCESS_SECRET=change_me_access_secret_min_32_chars
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change_me_refresh_secret_min_32_chars
JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES=15m
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES=7d

# Multi-tenant SaaS
DEFAULT_TENANT_SLUG=cubic
DEFAULT_TENANT_NAME=Cubic Studio
DEFAULT_TENANT_SEATS=100
# Email to promote as Editco platform admin (optional; else first admin user)
PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAIL=aanya@cubic.studio
# Set true only for local testing of open signup
ALLOW_PUBLIC_REGISTER=false

# Optional Google Calendar
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5000/api/calendar/google/callback
```

`CLIENT_URL` may be comma-separated for multiple frontends:
`CLIENT_URL=http://localhost:5173,https://your-app.vercel.app`

### client/.env

```
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000/api
VITE_TENANT_SLUG=cubic
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
```

## Production (Vercel + Render)

### Render (API) env

| Key | Example |
|-----|---------|
| `NODE_ENV` | `production` |
| `PORT` | `10000` (Render sets this; keep in sync) |
| `MONGODB_URI` | your Atlas connection string |
| `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET` | long random secret |
| `JWT_REFRESH_SECRET` | long random secret |
| `CLIENT_URL` | `https://your-app.vercel.app` |
| `DEFAULT_TENANT_SLUG` | `cubic` |
| `PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAIL` | your Editco admin email |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` | optional |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` | optional |
| `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` | `https://<render-host>/api/calendar/google/callback` |

### Vercel (frontend) env

| Key | Example |
|-----|---------|
| `VITE_API_URL` | `/api` (with vercel.json proxy) or full Render `/api` URL |
| `VITE_TENANT_SLUG` | `cubic` (fallback when not on subdomain) |
| `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` | same OAuth web client ID (optional) |

See [DEPLOY.md](DEPLOY.md) for the full checklist.

## Multi-tenant notes

- One MongoDB database; isolation via `tenantId` on documents.
- Workspace slug via subdomain (`acme.editcomedia.com`) or `X-Tenant-Slug` header / login field.
- Platform Admin UI: `/platform` (requires `isPlatformAdmin`).
- Seat limit enforced on invite / platform user create (default 30 per new tenant).

## Notes

- File uploads are stored on the API disk under `/uploads`. On Render’s free plan the disk is **ephemeral** (cleared on redeploy).
- Cloudinary / S3 can be wired later for durable storage.
